{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1481716-learning-changing-breed-s-gifts-and-vice-versa","id":1481716,"title":"Learning Changing Breed's Gifts and Vice-Versa","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-22T19:42:53-07:00","id":1481716,"title":"Learning Changing Breed's Gifts and Vice-Versa","content":"So, I was in a discussion with some friends who play RPG in the WoD and we got into this topic: Can a Garou learn other Changing Breed's gifts and vice-versa, i.e. can Changing Breeds learn Garou gifts?<br /> <br /> While I'm of the opinion that yes, they can, as I don't see any big problem and in fact many gifts are already shared by both Garou and Changing Breeds, e.g. Thieving Talons of the Magpie, Scrying, etc. My friend thinks that unless mentioned in the books, it shouldn't be possible (he's been a rules lawyer, lol).<br /> <br /> To sum up, that made me curious to listen to other opinions, what do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T20:08:48-07:00","id":1481719,"title":"","content":"IIRC the Revised CB book specifies that you can learn up to Rank 3 Gifts from other changers... so that right there should be pretty slam dunk on the rules lawyer thing.<br /> <br /> There are also a number of changers that don't learn Gifts from spirits, but have to learn them via direct instruction, or observing others using those Gifts (and are not limited to their own kind).<br /> <br /> So, in general? Yeah, you can learn Gifts from others. The big stipulations are:<br /> <br /> 1) Does the Gift rely on something that only that changer type can use? The Corax Gifts that weaponize feathers require having feather so... baring a handful of Mokole... nobody else can learn them. Ananasi and Gifts that require spending blood. Najah venom Gifts (which don't don't even work for them in Homid). Etc.<br /> <br /> 2) Is the Gift something considered a guarded secret in the lore of the game?<br /> <br /> 3) How do they know to even try? Just because a Qualmi can learn a Rokea Gift mechanically, there's a lot of explaining of how they even know about the Gift to try.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T20:24:07-07:00","id":1481721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> IIRC the Revised CB book specifies that you can learn up to Rank 3 Gifts from other changers... so that right there should be pretty slam dunk on the rules lawyer thing. </div> </div> </div>I wish I had used this information in the argument, but I sincerely didn't know it was mentioned in the books in such crystal clear form. Naturally, I agree with you that it wouldn't make sense for a Garou to use a gift that requires some inherent trait of another Changing Breed to work, as you mentioned, but the example I used, i.e. Luna's armor, I don't see any problem in a Corax or any other Changing Breed for the matter, to learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T12:46:14-07:00","id":1482282,"title":"","content":"Usually the In-Character limitations are enough to make it rare, but no rule states it to be impossible and, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, this is actually supposed to happen from time to time.<br /> <br /> If a Gift isn't in your personal lists of Gifts it means you have a list of considerations to make, but they don't change much if the Gift is from another Fera or whatever:<ul><li><b><u>No spirit is required to teach it by standard Chiminage or at all</u></b>;</li> <li><b><u>It may depend on features you don't have</u></b>;</li> <li><b><u>You don't necessarily know it exists or where to learn it</u></b>;</li> <li><b><u>Learning it <i>may</i> not be tolerated by some groups</u></b>;</li> <li><b><u>Teachers from other Breeds may raise the difficulty of learning</u></b>;</li> <li><b><u>Sometimes it isn't the same level for you as in the original list</u></b>.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> And that's about it. In practice going after even one of those is a challenge in itself, and may bring several difficulties even afterwards. But it doesn't have to, and once everything is in place it is unnecessary to just make it impossible.<br /> <br /> Gifts are supernatural powers granted by the spiritual nature of the Changing Breeds. Even when they depend on some specific feature it is not that the power comes from the feature, but just that it affects it. Ananasi with Venom or Web Gifts are as naturally able to produce large quantities of web or human-harming venom as a common spider, which for this purposes is barely better than a wolf. The Gift enhances those properties as unnaturally as a werewolf's claws becoming pure silver. They're all half-spirit. They're all able to learn Gifts equally. Even learning a Gift based on enhancing your feathers without having feathers is theoretically possible, just irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}